    "note": "candidate-002 — SHIP-READINESS check for @m0saic/alpine/progress-card/v1. The look is approved (multi-color + right-aligned values, per your verdict). This is the 'good to LOCK?' gate.\n\nALSO FIXED — your editor-affordance note: the objectRows Items editor squeezed the Label (text) column to an unusable sliver because the narrow inspector + 4 columns (Label/Value/Max/Color) left no room. Fixed app-side: the text cell now keeps a usable min-width (96px) and the row wraps instead of collapsing — so it renders well for the progress Items (and any many-column objectRows). Reload Make to see it.\n\nPRE-VERIFIED by me (real renders): 4-item default, 8 dense items (palette cycles, readable), max-based with valueLabel '680 / 1000 GB' on dark preset, >100% clamps, empty→error. \n\nHIGH-VALUE KNOBS WORTH YOUR EYES:\n  • value/max vs bare % ; a custom valueLabel ($ / GB / 'x of y').\n  • 1 item vs 8 items — row spacing + bar thickness.\n  • barColor (one color for ALL bars) vs per-item colors vs a CLEARED color (should fall back, not vanish).\n  • showValue off ; cornerRadius (square ↔ pill bars).\n  • very long label / long valueLabel (fit:contain caps).\n  • dark preset ; intro length ; reduce motion (static final).",
    "question": "Stress it (now with a usable Items editor). If it holds, approve the TEMPLATE and I'll lock @m0saic/alpine/progress-card/v1 with the FULL agent.md closeout (unit test + CLI E2E + manifest + News + preview image/video/poster + master.mosaic(x) + postmortem.mosaicx). Anything off → point me at it."
